{
  "fix": "update",
  "version": "6.5.7",
  "quote": {"source": "S1", "text": "\"fixed\": \"6.5.7\""},
  "summary": "Update the elliptic npm package to version 6.5.7, which the advisory record gives as the fixed version: its function that reads DER-encoded ECDSA signatures (_importDER) returns false when the first byte of r or of s has its top bit set, a check that version 6.5.6 does not have."
}

{
  "decision": "no_test",
  "reason": "By the lab's reading of the code excerpts, the affected version wrongly reads a length only when it is padded with a leading zero byte and its value is above 0x7f (128 or more); the seven BER cases are rewrites of a P-256 signature whose lengths are 69, 32 and 33, so the three padded ones (9, 68, 115) stay below that line and the other four have no padded length. Showing this weakness needs a longer signature from a larger curve, and the building block cannot run another curve or a new case."
}

{
  "decision": "no_test",
  "reason": "The weakness is a missing length check when elliptic reads an EdDSA signature, but the only building block hands the program ECDSA P-256 signatures in DER form and cannot test any other signature scheme or curve. None of its 484 cases is an EdDSA signature, so none reaches the part of the library that has the weakness; the ECDSA cases with zero bytes added or removed go through a different signature reader and would be testing something else."
}
